<title>SINGAPORE: ST Automotive H1 net up 35 pct.</title>
<headline>ST Automotive H1 net up 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>					1996		   1995</p>
<p>    Net profit		    7.68    vs	   5.69</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	 6.39    vs	   4.74</p>
<p>    Turnover		    125.57    vs	  81.51</p>
<p>    Pretax operating profit   3.69    vs	   6.56</p>
<p>    Investment income	   0.73    vs	   0.42</p>
<p>    Other income		  2.55    vs	   1.10</p>
<p>    Share from associates     3.63    vs	  (0.20)</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		10.61    vs	   7.89</p>
<p>    Tax			     2.77    vs	   2.20</p>
<p>NOTE: Singapore Technologies Automotive Ltd said group results at the operating level were lower due to the absence of taxi rental income, promotion costs for the new Opel Vectra and set-up costs incurred by Tuk Tuk International.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
